.\" DO NOT MODIFY THIS FILE!  It was generated by help2man 1.49.3.
.TH SMBIOS-KEYBOARD-CTL "1" "December 2025" "smbios-keyboard-ctl 2.4.3" "User Commands"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
smbios-keyboard-ctl \- ../src/bin/smbios-keyboard-ctl
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.B smbios-keyboard-ctl

.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show program's version number and exit
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-info\fR
This will Display the Supported Features for Keyboard
illumination
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-get\-status\fR
This will Display the current Status of Keyboard
Illumination Settings
.TP
\fB\-\-set\-mode\fR
Option to set USER Selectable Keyboard Mode
.TP
\fB\-\-set\-trigger\fR
Option to set Trigger types for Keyboard Illumination
.TP
\fB\-\-set\-timeout\-battery\fR=\fI\,SET_TIMEOUT_BATTERY\/\fR
Set Keyboard Illumination Timeout Value (battery)
.TP
\fB\-\-set\-timeout\-ac\fR=\fI\,SET_TIMEOUT_AC\/\fR
Set Keyboard Illumination Timeout Value (ac)
.TP
\fB\-\-set\-level\fR=\fI\,SET_LEVEL\/\fR
Set Keyboard Illumination Level
.TP
\fB\-\-als\fR=\fI\,ALS_OPTION\/\fR
Set/Get ALS (Ambient Light Sensor Status and Control
Level)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Display more verbose output.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Minimize program output. Only errors and warnings are
displayed.
.TP
\fB\-\-trace\fR
Enable verbose function tracing.
.TP
\fB\-\-logconfig\fR=\fI\,LOGCONFIG\/\fR
Specify alternate config log.
.TP
\fB\-\-security\-key\fR=\fI\,SECURITY_KEY\/\fR
BIOS pre\-calculated security key.
.TP
\fB\-\-password\fR=\fI\,PASSWORD\/\fR
BIOS Setup password for set/activate operations.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-rawpassword\fR
Do not auto\-convert password to scancodes.
.TP
\fB\-\-memory\-dat\fR=\fI\,MEMORY_DAT\/\fR
Path to a memory dump file to use instead of real RAM
.TP
\fB\-\-cmos\-dat\fR=\fI\,CMOS_DAT\/\fR
Path to a CMOS dump file to use instead of real CMOS
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
The full documentation for
.B smbios-keyboard-ctl
is maintained as a Texinfo manual.  If the
.B info
and
.B smbios-keyboard-ctl
programs are properly installed at your site, the command
.IP
.B info smbios-keyboard-ctl
.PP
should give you access to the complete manual.
